# chat: a task typed into the composer passes the intake (mock: `coding_task`, TUI-DESIGN-2 §3.13) and starts a --mock run;
# the transcript shows the [you] bubble, [run] start, one [step N] line per step (compact, §4.5) and the run end; the
# placeholder flips to the follow-up form; /exit leaves 0 (§1, §8.2 chat-task)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.3
send fix the failing test
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*fix the failing test
expect step \d+/\d+
expect \[step 1\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
expect finished [·-] (complete|max_steps|generator_done)
expect Follow-up, question
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
